# Caddy automatically gets and renews a free HTTPS certificate (Let's
# Encrypt) for whatever domain you put here, the first time it starts --
# nothing else to configure. Replace the line below with your real domain
# (it must already point at this server's IP in DNS before Caddy starts,
# or the certificate request will fail).
#
# No domain yet? Use a free wildcard DNS service that resolves straight
# to the IP in its own hostname, e.g. your server's IP 203.0.113.5 as
# 203-0-113-5.nip.io -- no DNS setup needed, no account, works instantly.
# Get HTTPS working today with that, swap in a real domain later without
# changing anything else here.

your-domain.example.com {
	reverse_proxy app:8080
}
